# LMD-GHOST Fork-Choice Estimator — Formal Verification
#
# Mechanizes the GHOST-style heaviest-subtree fork-choice estimator and the
# properties on which its consensus-critical correctness rests: one complete
# certified latest-message slot per frozen-floor authority, floor-descendant
# vote eligibility, receiver-local-state noninterference, frozen authority
# weights, score order-independence, the (score DESC, hash ASC) total order,
# LMD upward argmax termination and heaviest-child selection, parent-count and
# parent-depth truncation, and the "Rocq assumes what Rust enforces" seams.
#
# Source: f1r3node-rust/casper/src/rust/{estimator,validate}.rs,
#         casper/src/rust/engine/multi_parent_casper/snapshot.rs,
#         casper/src/rust/causal_equivocation.rs,
#         casper/src/rust/util/dag_operations.rs,
#         shared/src/rust/shared/list_ops.rs (sort_by_with_decreasing_order).
#
# Zero `Admitted`. No custom `Axiom` or `Parameter`. Section `Variable`/
# `Hypothesis` (GuardBridge, as in finalized_floor) become premises of the
# closed term, NOT axioms.
#
# Fork choice is a stateless derivation from a certified round context. Crash
# atomicity and effect idempotence belong to the finalized-floor development.
#
# Module dependency graph (-> = "depends on"):
#
#   Foundation            (standalone: DAG, block numbers, parents, ancestry, height bound)
#   Score      -> Foundation                 (per-validator weight, supporting-chain scores)
#   Filter     -> Foundation                 (certified eligibility projection)
#   CertifiedContext -> Foundation           (complete slots, floor ancestry, locality)
#   TieBreak   -> Foundation                 (the (score DESC, hash ASC) TOTAL order + unique sort — S1)
#   Lca        -> Foundation                 (LCUA over all certified eligible messages)
#   Rank       -> Foundation Score TieBreak   (LMD upward argmax descent: terminates, picks heaviest)
#   TerminalFrontier -> Foundation Rank TieBreak (exact concurrent frontier + GHOST-head composition)
#   Bound      -> Foundation Rank            (parent-count cap: keeps the ghost main parent; typed empty err)
#   ParentAntichain -> Foundation             (reachability-maximal compaction + coverage guard)
#   GuardBridge-> Foundation Rank Bound Filter Score TieBreak  (validation⇒wf; honest parents validate)
#   MainTheorem-> all                        (five end-to-end capstones, axiom-free)

